  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "style": "CardLabel",
      "text": "REPEATING RULES / PRACTICE SET"
    },
    {
      "style": "Title",
      "text": "Pattern Practice Cards"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading1",
      "text": "Four short activities for noticing and using a repeating rule."
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "Who and why"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Teacher-supported beginners, approximately ages 7–9. Assume learners can distinguish the three printed…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Learner evidence: name a stated unit, extend it in order, repair one mismatch, then create and test a…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "Use the cards"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Use the four task fronts and matching demonstration backs, paper and a pencil if useful. Shape key: ○…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Begin with card 01. Model one unit on its back when needed, then let each learner try. Use 02 and 03…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Planning estimate: 3–5 minutes per activity, plus setup and discussion. These times are adjustable and…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "Watch, coach and retry"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Ask: “What is the rule? Where does this position match it?” Name the specific mismatch, offer the shown…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Record only what you actually observe: independent, with support, needs another attempt, or not yet…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "Prepare the print set"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Print this setup page separately. Pages 2–5 are landscape Letter, two cards per sheet. For duplex, try…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Confirm that each front has the same numbered back and both read upright. A teacher cuts on the centre…"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardNote",
      "text": "Original teaching examples by Studio Templates. Shape rules are fully stated; there is no curriculum…"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardLabel",
      "text": "REPEATING RULES / PRACTICE SET"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardNumber",
      "text": "01"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardLabel",
      "text": "TASK FRONT"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading1",
      "text": "Find the repeat"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardLead",
      "text": "Name the repeating unit in order."
    },
    {
      "style": "CardBody",
      "text": "This pattern repeats a 2-shape unit. Start at the left."
    },
    {
      "style": "CardPattern",
      "text": "○ △ ○ △ ○ △"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "Try it"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardBody",
      "text": "Point to one complete unit. Say or draw its shapes in order, then show where the next copy starts."
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "Check your work"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardBody",
      "text": "I can name the unit and point to each matching copy."
    },
    {
      "style": "CardNote",
      "text": "Cover the later shapes if helpful. Move along one shape at a time."
    },
    {
      "style": "CardNote",
      "text": "My unit, in words or a sketch: __________________"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardLabel",
      "text": "REPEATING RULES / PRACTICE SET"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardNumber",
      "text": "02"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardLabel",
      "text": "TASK FRONT"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading1",
      "text": "Extend the rule"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardLead",
      "text": "Use the stated rule to add the next unit."
    },
    {
      "style": "CardBody",
      "text": "Repeat this unit in order: square, then circle."
    },
    {
      "style": "CardPattern",
      "text": "□ ○ □ ○ | __ __"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "Try it"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardBody",
      "text": "The first two units are shown. Say or draw the next 2 shapes. Explain how they follow the rule."
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "Check your work"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardBody",
      "text": "My added shapes copy the whole unit in the same order."
    },
    {
      "style": "CardNote",
      "text": "Touch the first unit, then copy it once into the blank space."
    },
    {
      "style": "CardNote",
      "text": "My next unit: ______________________________"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardLabel",
      "text": "REPEATING RULES / PRACTICE SET"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardNumber",
      "text": "02"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardLabel",
      "text": "DEMONSTRATION BACK"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading1",
      "text": "Copy the whole unit"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardPattern",
      "text": "□ ○ □ ○ □ ○"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardBody",
      "text": "The last unit is square, then circle. It matches the stated rule; it does not reverse the order."
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "If it does not match"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardBody",
      "text": "If the order changed, point to the first unit and match each new position to it. Then retry with the…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "Try a new input"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardBody",
      "text": "New rule: repeat circle, then square. Add one unit."
    },
    {
      "style": "CardPattern",
      "text": "○ □ ○ □ | __ __"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardNote",
      "text": "Check: add circle, then square."
    },
    {
      "style": "CardLabel",
      "text": "REPEATING RULES / PRACTICE SET"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardNumber",
      "text": "01"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardLabel",
      "text": "DEMONSTRATION BACK"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading1",
      "text": "A unit repeats as a group"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardPattern",
      "text": "○ △"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardBody",
      "text": "Read from the left: circle, then triangle. This whole group appears three times in the task pattern."
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "If it does not match"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardBody",
      "text": "If you named just the last shape, return to the start. Group the shapes that repeat together and try…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "Try a new input"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardBody",
      "text": "New pattern: find its 2-shape unit. Try before checking the line below."
    },
    {
      "style": "CardPattern",
      "text": "△ ○ △ ○ △ ○"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardNote",
      "text": "Check: triangle, then circle. Point to all three copies."
    },
    {
      "style": "CardLabel",
      "text": "REPEATING RULES / PRACTICE SET"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardNumber",
      "text": "03"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardLabel",
      "text": "TASK FRONT"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading1",
      "text": "Repair one break"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardLead",
      "text": "Find and change the one shape that breaks the rule."
    },
    {
      "style": "CardBody",
      "text": "Rule: repeat triangle, then square. One shape below is wrong."
    },
    {
      "style": "CardPattern",
      "text": "△ □ △ △ △ □"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "Try it"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardBody",
      "text": "Count positions from the left, starting at one. Name the position to change and the shape that belongs…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "Check your work"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardBody",
      "text": "One change makes all three units follow the stated rule."
    },
    {
      "style": "CardNote",
      "text": "Compare each group of 2 positions with the rule. Keep shapes that already match."
    },
    {
      "style": "CardNote",
      "text": "Change position ______ to ____________________"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardLabel",
      "text": "REPEATING RULES / PRACTICE SET"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardNumber",
      "text": "04"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardLabel",
      "text": "TASK FRONT"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading1",
      "text": "Make and test a rule"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardLead",
      "text": "State a rule and show three matching copies."
    },
    {
      "style": "CardBody",
      "text": "Choose two different shapes. Put one of each in order to make a two-shape unit."
    },
    {
      "style": "CardPattern",
      "text": "○ △ □"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "Try it"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardBody",
      "text": "Choose from circle, triangle and square. Say your unit, then draw or name three copies in order. A…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "Check your work"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardBody",
      "text": "My unit fits the rule, and every copy keeps its order."
    },
    {
      "style": "CardNote",
      "text": "Keep your first unit visible while you make the next two copies."
    },
    {
      "style": "CardNote",
      "text": "My unit and three copies: ____________________"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardLabel",
      "text": "REPEATING RULES / PRACTICE SET"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardNumber",
      "text": "04"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardLabel",
      "text": "DEMONSTRATION BACK"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading1",
      "text": "One possible answer"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardPattern",
      "text": "□ △ □ △ □ △"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardBody",
      "text": "Example unit: square, triangle. Other answers work when they fit the task rule and repeat correctly."
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "If it does not match"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardBody",
      "text": "If a copy changes order, compare it with your stated unit and revise that copy. A different valid unit…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "Try a new input"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardBody",
      "text": "Change context: use two different letters as your unit. Repeat the unit three times."
    },
    {
      "style": "CardPattern",
      "text": "A B | A B | A B"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardNote",
      "text": "The printed letter line is one model. Make a different valid letter unit, then check all three copies…"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardLabel",
      "text": "REPEATING RULES / PRACTICE SET"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardNumber",
      "text": "03"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardLabel",
      "text": "DEMONSTRATION BACK"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading1",
      "text": "Check positions against the rule"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardPattern",
      "text": "△ □ △ □ △ □"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardBody",
      "text": "Change position 4 to square. All other positions already match the rule. The line above is the repaired…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "If it does not match"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardBody",
      "text": "If you changed several shapes, reset to the task line. Compare one position at a time; the task needs…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "Try a new input"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardBody",
      "text": "New rule: repeat circle, then triangle. Find one wrong shape."
    },
    {
      "style": "CardPattern",
      "text": "○ △ ○ ○ ○ △"
    },
    {
      "style": "CardNote",
      "text": "Check: change position 4 to triangle."
    }
  ],
